  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is positive (0.00–0.67) and model shows over-optimism (e.g., overshoots recent highs).",
    "Reduce forecast volatility in early horizon (1–7 days) when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive; avoid sharp upward moves.",
    "When sentiment peaks (0.67+) and price spikes, cap forecast increase to avoid overcorrection; allow gradual mean reversion.",
    "In high sentiment (0.50+) periods, model tends to overestimate short-term price stability — apply slight downward bias to align with true mean reversion.",
    "If model consistently overpredicts 30-day outcomes (e.g., +2–3% above true), apply a 1–2% downward adjustment to future forecasts.",
    "Lagging sentiment (e.g., 0.00–0.25) correlates with underestimation — increase forecast by 0.5–1.0% to compensate for delayed reaction."
  ]
}
